reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:16:| Setting | `renewals.spread_window_hours`, default **6** | `arraysubs/src/functions/renewal-spread-helpers.php:48` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:17:| Stored on this site? | **No** — key absent from `arraysubs_settings`, so the default 6 applies (verified: `wp eval 'arraysubs_get_setting("renewals.spread_window_hours",6)' --allow-root` → `6`) | live check |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:18:| Window cap | `min(configured_hours, floor(cycle_hours*3600/4))` — 25% of the billing cycle | `renewal-spread-helpers.php:63-70` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:19:| Effective window | For any cycle ≥ 1 day this evaluates to **21600 s (6 h)** (day cycle = 24h → 24*3600/4 = 21600) | `renewal-spread-helpers.php:66-69` + `RenewalScheduler::getBillingCycleInHours()` `arraysubs/src/Features/RecurringBilling/Services/RenewalScheduler.php:222-235` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:20:| Offset formula | `offset = ((int) sprintf('%u', crc32('arraysubs-spread-' . $subscription_id))) % $window`, filterable via `arraysubs_renewal_spread_offset`, clamped to ≥ 0 | `renewal-spread-helpers.php:88-108` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:25:php -r 'foreach([100,101,1234,5000] as $id){$h=(int)sprintf("%u",crc32("arraysubs-spread-".$id));printf("id=%d offset=%ds (%s)\n",$id,$h%21600,gmdate("H:i:s",$h%21600));}'
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:32:`_next_payment_date` itself is **never** shifted by the spread — only the Action Scheduler execution timestamps.
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:36:Let `D` = `_next_payment_date` (UTC MySQL string on the `arraysubs_data` post), `k` = spread offset (seconds), `L` = invoice lead = **6 h** here.
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:40:| `D + k − L` = **D + k − 6h** | `arraysubs_generate_renewal_invoice` [`$subscription_id`] fires | scheduled at `RenewalScheduler::scheduleInvoice()` `RenewalScheduler.php:135-156`; timestamp from `getInvoiceTimestamp()` `RenewalScheduler.php:165-188` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:41:| ↳ | Handler re-checks: post status ∈ {`arraysubs-active`,`arraysubs-trial`}, no existing pending renewal order, `shouldGenerateInvoiceNow()`, filter `arraysubs_should_generate_renewal_invoice` | `arraysubs/src/Features/RecurringBilling/Services/Hooks.php:1177-1215` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:42:| ↳ | `RenewalProcessor::createRenewalInvoice()` → `OrderCreation::createRenewalOrder()` creates a WooCommerce order with `status = pending` | `RenewalProcessor.php:34-131`, `OrderCreation.php:88-90` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:44:| ↳ | Subscription meta `_pending_renewal_order_id` set; **subscription status is NOT changed** (stays active/trial through the whole grace period) | `RenewalProcessor.php:114-122` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:45:| ↳ | `do_action('arraysubs_renewal_invoice_created', $sub_id, $order_id)` | `RenewalProcessor.php:125` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:48:| ↳ | Picks up the pending order (statuses pending/on-hold/failed, newest first); if none exists it creates one inline under the invoice lock | `RenewalProcessor.php:306-344`, `getPendingRenewalOrder()` `:822-874` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:49:| ↳ | If `_payment_retry_attempts > 0`: runs `arraysubs_pre_retry_charge_verification` first (never re-charges an already-charged cycle) | `RenewalProcessor.php:360-393` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:53:| ↳ | `_last_payment_date` set; `_completed_payments` incremented **only when order total > 0**; `_pending_renewal_order_id` and `_on_hold_date` deleted; all retry meta cleared | `OrderIntegration.php:1153-1188` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:57:| ↳ | `do_action('arraysubs_renewal_payment_complete')` → payment-successful email + renewal reminder rescheduled | `OrderIntegration.php:1236`; `EmailManager::on_renewal_payment_complete()` `arraysubs/src/Features/Emails/Services/EmailManager.php:524-546` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:59:## 2. How `invoice_before_due` = 6 hours is actually applied
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:61:`arraysubs_get_invoice_hours_before_due()` converts value+unit → hours (`value*24` when unit = `days`): `arraysubs/src/functions/settings-helpers.php:735-745`. Site value: `6` + `hours` → **6**.
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:68:   - `invoice_ts = (D + k) − lead*3600`
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:69:   - **Guard**: `if (invoice_ts <= time() && D+k > time()) return time() + 60;` — i.e. when you time-travel a due date to "6 h from now or less", the invoice job is queued for **now + 1 minute**, not in the past.
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:71:3. **Hourly recovery sweep** `doGenerateUpcomingRenewalsBatch()` (`Hooks.php:389-495`) — SQL cutoff is `now + 6h`, then a **spread-aware skip**: `if (now < due_ts + offset − effective_hours*3600) continue;` (`Hooks.php:446-459`).
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:77:| Renewal WC order | `pending` (created) → `processing`/`completed` (paid) or `failed` (charge declined, `RenewalProcessor.php:594-597`) or `cancelled` (subscription cancelled for non-payment, `RenewalProcessor.php:258`) |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:78:| Subscription | `arraysubs-active` throughout invoice + first grace window → `arraysubs-on-hold` (sweep phase 1) → `arraysubs-cancelled` (sweep phase 2). Registered slugs: `arraysubs-pending`, `arraysubs-active`, `arraysubs-on-hold`, `arraysubs-cancelled`, `arraysubs-expired`, `arraysubs-trial` — `arraysubs/src/Features/Subscriptions/Services/SubscriptionCPT.php:94-156` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:84:For an automatic-payment subscription with auto-renew on, `EmailManager::on_renewal_invoice_created()` **returns without sending the renewal-invoice email** (`EmailManager.php:495-513`). So on Stripe the customer sees nothing at `D+k−6h`; the first mail is the payment-successful (or payment-failed) email at `D+k`. On bacs/cheque/cod or `_auto_renew='off'`, the invoice email *does* go out at `D+k−6h`.

